# What ships in a public release.
#
# scripts/release.sh builds every published snapshot from `git archive
# HEAD`, and git archive honours `export-ignore`. Anything marked here is
# therefore absent from the snapshot by construction -- no script logic to
# keep in step, and it keeps working if the snapshot method ever changes.
#
# backlog/ is this repo's own Backlog.md board: the development history of
# the project, written for the maintainer rather than for a reader of the
# published source. Agents working here routinely write filesystem paths
# and cross-repo references into task notes, so it is not a surface a
# one-time scrub could keep clean. See the decision record filed with
# TASK-101 for what this costs and when a curated subset might ship.
backlog/ export-ignore
